<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64050" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λύδιος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῡ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of
				Lydia, Lydian</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					5.19
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύκινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
					33.12
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>VH</u>
				1.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Harm.</u>
				1
			</span></i>: prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρὰ τὸ Λύδιον ἅρμα
				θέειν</span>
			<i>to be left far behind</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diogenian.
				6.28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Greg.Cypr.
				2.99
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				206
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λυδία λίθος, ἡ</span>, a siliceous stone used to assay gold, and
			first discovered in Lydia, elsewhere 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάσανος, Λυδία γὰρ λίθος μανύει
					χρυσόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					10
				</span></i>
			; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λ. πέτρη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					12.36
				</span></i>
			; and 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anon.
				</span></i>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				<u>An.Ox.</u>
				3.216
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λ. λίθος</span>, of the magnet,
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				800
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λύδιον, τό</span>, a kind of vase, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λ. μέζω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AJA</u>
					31.349
				</span></i>
			.</div>
